a figure of speech which, by describing the {#aprastuta#}
 (what is not the subject-matter) conveys a reference to the {#prastuta#}
 or subject-matter; {#aprastutapraSaMsA sA yA sEva prastutASrayA#} <ls>K. P. 10</ls>.
 It is of 5 kinds:-- {#kArye nimitte sAmAnye viSeze prastute sati .#}
 {#tadanyasya vacastulye tulyasyeti ca paYcaDA ..#} {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} when the subject-matter is viewed
.³({%a%}) as an effect, information of which is conveyed by stating the cause;
.³({%b%}) when viewed as a cause by stating the effect;
.³({%c%}) when viewed as a general assertion by stating a particular instance;
.³({%d%}) when viewed as a particular instance by stating a general assertion; and
.³({%e%}) when viewed as similar by stating what is similar to it. See
 <ls>K. P. 10</ls> and <ls>S. D. 706</ls> for examples.
